# No stubs / empty chrome

If something is shown to the user (button, checkbox, mode, scenario, mic, record), it must be a **working path** — not a placeholder, dead wire, or half-hook.

## Forbidden

- Buttons that open nothing, log slogans, or promise a mode that is not wired
- Checkboxes for recording/preview that produce empty/broken files while looking “on”
- Scenario/role pickers that do not load a real pack and character sheet
- Voice/mic UI without SpeechRecognition (or honest “недоступно в этом браузере”)
- Reading system prompts / JSON schema / WANT/MISSION aloud as dialogue
- Fake “success” when the actor did not act in the world

## Required

- One clear primary loop: live role ↔ viewer (text and/or mic) ↔ embodied action + speech
- Ready packs that ship in UI must load worlds + roles that play
- Recording: only offer modes that actually write usable media; prefer one solid path over two broken ones
- If a capability is missing — hide the control or show a short honest reason (no fake enable)

## Default

Prefer deleting a half-button over shipping it “for later”.
